===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|orv|красьнъ}}, {{m|orv|красьнꙑи||beautiful, good}}, from {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*krasьnъ||beautiful}}. The sense “red” is unique to Russian and did not develop in other Slavic descendants of {{m|sla-pro|*krasьnъ}}; first attested in 1515 in Muscovite diplomatic correspondence, it serves as the primary sense of the word in the modern Russian language.

For sense development, compare {{m|ru|кра́ска|t=paint}}, original sense hypothesized to be “blush” or “decoration”, and to {{m|ru|кра́сить|t=to color}}, original sense “to decorate”.

Also compare {{ncog|vot|kauniz}}.

